/-
# Chamber certificate, part 3: the Farey-29 chambers and the per-chamber arithmetic check

`farey` lists the `271` Farey fractions of order `29` in `[0,1]`; the `270` chambers are the open
intervals between consecutive ones.  For chamber `i` with left endpoint `a/b` the data is
`wOf a b c = ⌊c a / b⌋` (`= ⌊cN/p⌋` for every `N/p` in the chamber).  `chamberOK i` checks, by
natural-number arithmetic only, that `certI ≤ e₀ + 𝟙_{x > 1/19}` and `certP ≤ e₁ + 1`, where
`(e₀, e₁)` are the entries of the table row `rowN i` containing the chamber (`ptableN` is
`profileTable` with the rationals written as pairs), that the chamber lies in that row and is
disjoint from the other rows, and that no fraction of denominator `≤ 29` lies inside the chamber.
The `270` checks `chamber_i` are in `Chamber_cert0.lean`, …, `Chamber_cert9.lean`.
-/
